2026-09-12 06:02:35 EDT [CRAWLER] St Barbara has entered into a binding agreement to divest its remaining stake in the New Simberi Gold Project to Lingbao Gold Group for A$410m in cash.  
2026-09-12 06:02:35 EDT [CRAWLER] In addition to the cash consideration, St Barbara will receive a further A$43m cash repayment for its share of construction capital for New Simberi between April 2026 and the agreement signing.  
2026-09-12 06:02:35 EDT [CRAWLER] Lingbao will also cover St Barbara's share of capital requirements for New Simberi from the signing of the agreement until completion.  
2026-09-12 06:02:35 EDT [CRAWLER] If the deal does not complete due to certain conditions not being satisfied by Lingbao, this funding becomes a loan repayable by St Barbara.  
2026-09-12 06:02:35 EDT [CRAWLER] Upon completion, St Barbara will retain a 2.75% net smelter return (NSR) royalty on future gold and silver production from New Simberi, as well as a 1.5% royalty on any future minerals output from the Tabar Islands Group exploration licences.  
2026-09-12 06:02:35 EDT [CRAWLER] Both royalty payments are due to begin from 1 July 2027, with Lingbao providing a parent company guarantee.  
